{"id": "2026-11-10-news-abu-dhabi-talks-open-on-ukraine-s-borders", "date": "2026-11-10", "stream": "news", "headline": "Abu Dhabi talks open on Ukraine's borders", "summary": "Russian, Ukrainian and US delegations began two days of talks in Abu Dhabi on Tuesday 10 November, the first three-way meeting since February, after US, European and Ukrainian officials issued a joint statement that any deal must respect Ukraine's \"territorial integrity\".", "url": "https://www.lemonde.fr/international/live/2026/11/10/en-direct-guerre-en-ukraine-tout-accord-sur-l-ukraine-doit-respecter-son-integrite-territoriale-affirment-europeens-et-americains_6808609_3210.html", "source_domain": "lemonde.fr", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["geopolitics"], "importance": 3, "display_body": "Russian, Ukrainian and US delegations began two days of talks in Abu Dhabi on Tuesday 10 November, the first three-way meeting since February, after US, European and Ukrainian officials issued a joint statement that any deal must respect Ukraine's \"territorial integrity\". The statement, relayed by the European Commission after a meeting ahead of the talks, says any future agreement must respect Ukraine's \"sovereignty, territorial integrity and independence of decision\" and give it \"credible security guarantees\". It also commits the participants to a \"strong\" European security set-up after the war. The talks run on Tuesday 10 and Wednesday 11 November under US envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner. Le Temps notes that the Europeans are present only on the margins, and that the Kremlin prefers to negotiate without the EU. Russia struck energy infrastructure in eight Ukrainian regions overnight, according to grid operator Ukrenergo, and Denmark announced about €640 million in new military aid as Volodymyr Zelensky arrived in Copenhagen.", "why": "Europe's written red line on borders now has US signatures on it, and these two days will show whether Moscow accepts talks on that basis.", "thread_id": "2026-11-10-news-abu-dhabi-talks-open-on-ukraine-s-borders", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-10", "event_date": "2026-11-10", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Ukraine", "Russia", "United States", "Abu Dhabi", "European Union"]}
{"id": "2026-11-10-news-trump-calls-iran-war-militarily-over", "date": "2026-11-10", "stream": "news", "headline": "Trump calls Iran war militarily over", "summary": "After meeting Qatar's prime minister at the White House on Monday 9 November, Donald Trump said he saw \"positive momentum\" towards a deal with Iran and called the war \"militarily over\".", "url": "https://www.lemonde.fr/international/article/2026/11/10/donald-trump-evoque-un-elan-positif-vers-un-accord-de-paix-avec-l-iran-apres-sa-rencontre-avec-le-premier-ministre-du-qatar_6808708_3210.html", "source_domain": "lemonde.fr", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["single-source"], "topics": ["geopolitics"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "After meeting Qatar's prime minister at the White House on Monday 9 November, Donald Trump said he saw \"positive momentum\" towards a deal with Iran and called the war \"militarily over\". In the same breath he said the US remains \"ready to intervene\", and that a return to strikes is \"unlikely\" rather than ruled out. Tehran's account differs. Mohsen Rezaei, secretary of Iran's Supreme National Security Council, told the US to \"stop fabricating\" news of \"imaginary\" talks. Iranian authorities also say strikes the US military has not announced are continuing: the island of Qeshm in the Strait of Hormuz was hit overnight from Sunday to Monday, according to the provincial deputy governor.", "why": "Trump's \"over\" sits alongside reported strikes and a denial from Tehran, so treat it as his own description, not an established ceasefire.", "thread_id": "2026-11-10-news-trump-calls-iran-war-militarily-over", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-10", "event_date": "2026-11-09", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Donald Trump", "Iran", "Qatar", "Qeshm"]}
{"id": "2026-11-10-news-france-summons-iran-envoy-over-fridge-sabotage", "date": "2026-11-10", "stream": "news", "headline": "France summons Iran envoy over fridge sabotage", "summary": "France summoned Iran's ambassador on Tuesday 10 November, a day after it blamed Iran's Revolutionary Guards for remotely sabotaging refrigeration in more than 700 French supermarkets on 11 and 12 October.", "url": "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/11/10/france-summons-irans-ambassador-over-supermarket-fridge-sabotage", "source_domain": "aljazeera.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["single-source"], "topics": ["geopolitics", "security"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "France summoned Iran's ambassador on Tuesday 10 November, a day after it blamed Iran's Revolutionary Guards for remotely sabotaging refrigeration in more than 700 French supermarkets on 11 and 12 October. Foreign Minister Jean-Noël Barrot called it \"the first large-scale cyberattack aimed at sabotage on our national territory\" and said France will push for EU sanctions. The attackers triggered \"abnormal, indefinite defrost cycles\"; retailers including E.Leclerc, Intermarché and Carrefour say millions of euros of food spoiled, and some equipment caught fire. Paris prosecutor Laure Beccuau has opened an investigation into Shahid Kaveh, a cyber unit of the Guards, and requested international arrest warrants for two of its officials. Temperature spikes were also recorded in stores in Belgium, Estonia, Ireland, Luxembourg and Sweden on 2 November.", "why": "a state attribution for sabotage of civilian infrastructure inside the EU gives Brussels a sanctions decision to make, and the 2 November incidents suggest France is not the only target.", "thread_id": "2026-11-10-news-france-summons-iran-envoy-over-fridge-sabotage", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-10", "event_date": "2026-11-10", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["France", "Iran", "IRGC", "Shahid Kaveh", "Jean-Noël Barrot"]}
{"id": "2026-11-10-news-massie-files-hegseth-impeachment-articles", "date": "2026-11-10", "stream": "news", "headline": "Massie files Hegseth impeachment articles", "summary": "Republican congressman Thomas Massie introduced eight articles of impeachment against Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth on Monday 9 November, accusing him of waging the Iran war without congressional authorisation.", "url": "https://www.dw.com/en/us-pentagon-chief-hegseth-faces-impeachment-push-over-iran-war/a-79905323", "source_domain": "dw.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["single-source"], "topics": ["politics"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Republican congressman Thomas Massie introduced eight articles of impeachment against Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth on Monday 9 November, accusing him of waging the Iran war without congressional authorisation. Massie used a procedure that can force a House vote within two days, in a chamber Republicans control until 3 January. Trump said Hegseth had done a \"good job\". Hegseth scheduled a press conference for Tuesday 10 November, his first in more than 180 days. The move follows last week's midterms, in which Democrats won both chambers amid anger over the war and fuel prices. Impeachment needs a simple House majority; removal needs two-thirds of the Senate, which even the incoming Democratic majority cannot reach without substantial Republican support.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-11-10-news-massie-files-hegseth-impeachment-articles", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-10", "event_date": "2026-11-09", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Thomas Massie", "Pete Hegseth", "US House of Representatives"]}
{"id": "2026-11-10-news-novaya-gazeta-shuts-moscow-newsroom", "date": "2026-11-10", "stream": "news", "headline": "Novaya Gazeta shuts Moscow newsroom", "summary": "Novaya Gazeta, the independent Russian newspaper co-founded with Mikhail Gorbachev's Nobel money, closed its Moscow newsroom on Monday 9 November.", "url": "https://www.europarl.europa.eu/news/en/press-room/20261109IPR48724/", "source_domain": "europarl.europa.eu", "tier": "T1", "tags": [], "topics": ["politics"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "Novaya Gazeta, the independent Russian newspaper co-founded with Mikhail Gorbachev's Nobel money, closed its Moscow newsroom on Monday 9 November. The authorities had labelled it a \"foreign agent\", ordered it out of its offices and barred Russian banks from processing readers' donations. Kremlin spokesman Dmitry Peskov called the closure part of a \"rotational process\" in the media market. Three European Parliament office-holders called it \"the latest step by an authoritarian regime that fears its own citizens' access to the truth\" and urged the EU to fund and protect exiled Russian media, including Novaya Gazeta Europe.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-11-10-news-novaya-gazeta-shuts-moscow-newsroom", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-10", "event_date": "2026-11-09", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Novaya Gazeta", "Russia", "European Parliament", "Dmitry Muratov"]}
{"id": "2026-11-10-news-hackers-seek-ransom-over-federal-staff-data", "date": "2026-11-10", "stream": "news", "headline": "Hackers seek ransom over federal staff data", "summary": "The Akira hacker group demanded a ransom after stealing data from a software supplier to Publica, the federal staff pension fund, and the stolen files may cover all federal employees, including intelligence and police officers working under false identities, SRF reported on Tuesday 10 November.", "url": "https://www.srf.ch/news/schweiz/heikle-daten-gestohlen-hacker-fordern-loesegeld-nach-angriff-auf-publica-lieferantin", "source_domain": "srf.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["single-source"], "topics": ["switzerland", "security"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "The Akira hacker group demanded a ransom after stealing data from a software supplier to Publica, the federal staff pension fund, and the stolen files may cover all federal employees, including intelligence and police officers working under false identities, SRF reported on Tuesday 10 November. Several sources confirmed to SRF that the Defence Department (DDPS) knows about the extortion. The supplier, PK Softech AG, and Publica both say they received no ransom demand themselves, which suggests it went straight to the federal government. The Federal Council discussed the case in secret last Wednesday, 4 November, its spokesperson confirmed, without giving details. The Office of the Attorney General named Akira as the attacker more than two weeks ago.", "why": "the government advises everyone else never to pay, but state-owned Ruag paid Akira last year, so how Bern handles this demand will be watched closely.", "thread_id": "2026-11-10-news-hackers-seek-ransom-over-federal-staff-data", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-10", "event_date": "2026-11-10", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Publica", "Akira", "DDPS", "Federal Council"]}
{"id": "2026-11-10-news-private-donors-to-back-2038-olympic-deficit", "date": "2026-11-10", "stream": "news", "headline": "Private donors to back 2038 Olympic deficit", "summary": "The Switzerland 2038 Winter Olympics bid plans a CHF 200 million deficit guarantee funded entirely by private donors and companies, with no state backstop, SRF reported on Tuesday 10 November.", "url": "https://www.srf.ch/news/wirtschaft/olympia-in-der-schweiz-private-defizit-garantie-fuer-olympia-in-der-schweiz", "source_domain": "srf.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["single-source"], "topics": ["switzerland", "sports"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "The Switzerland 2038 Winter Olympics bid plans a CHF 200 million deficit guarantee funded entirely by private donors and companies, with no state backstop, SRF reported on Tuesday 10 November. The bid's budget is CHF 2.2 billion, of which CHF 1.8 billion would come from private money and ticket sales, with CHF 200 million from the Confederation and CHF 200 million from cantons and communes. The National Council has approved the federal share; the Council of States decides in December. The bid must be filed by February 2027. CIPRA Switzerland, an Alpine-protection group, says Winter Games budgets usually double and the guarantee should double too.", "why": "the private guarantee is the bid's answer to the cost argument that has sunk earlier Swiss Olympic bids at the ballot box.", "thread_id": "2026-11-10-news-private-donors-to-back-2038-olympic-deficit", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-10", "event_date": null, "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Switzerland 2038", "Council of States", "CIPRA"]}
{"id": "2026-11-10-news-swiss-national-roads-hold-steady-rating", "date": "2026-11-10", "stream": "news", "headline": "Swiss national roads hold steady rating", "summary": "The Federal Roads Office (FEDRO/OFROU) rated the national road network at 1.81 on a scale from 1 (good) to 5 (alarming) in its 2025 condition report, published on Tuesday 10 November, unchanged from a year earlier.", "url": "https://www.admin.ch/fr/newnsb/46enzWKETnBy", "source_domain": "admin.ch", "tier": "T1", "tags": ["official PR", "new source"], "topics": ["switzerland"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "The Federal Roads Office (FEDRO/OFROU) rated the national road network at 1.81 on a scale from 1 (good) to 5 (alarming) in its 2025 condition report, published on Tuesday 10 November, unchanged from a year earlier. About 97% of road surfaces are good or average. Three tunnels got poor marks: Solis and Passmal in Graubünden and Schwarzwald in Basel; their repair is planned or under way, and FEDRO says they remain safe to use. Maintenance cost about CHF 1.26 billion in 2025, and about CHF 1.19 billion a year is planned for 2026–2030. It is paid entirely from earmarked road-user charges, not the general federal budget.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-11-10-news-swiss-national-roads-hold-steady-rating", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-10", "event_date": "2026-11-10", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["FEDRO"]}
{"id": "2026-11-10-news-swiss-fund-unhcr-evacuations-in-ukraine", "date": "2026-11-10", "stream": "news", "headline": "Swiss fund UNHCR evacuations in Ukraine", "summary": "Switzerland is giving CHF 4 million to the UN refugee agency (UNHCR) to help evacuate people from front-line areas of Ukraine, the Federal Council's Ukraine delegate Jacques Gerber announced in Kyiv on Monday 9 November.", "url": "https://www.admin.ch/fr/newnsb/fxWFBZ1Zd6h4", "source_domain": "admin.ch", "tier": "T1", "tags": ["official PR"], "topics": ["switzerland", "geopolitics"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "Switzerland is giving CHF 4 million to the UN refugee agency (UNHCR) to help evacuate people from front-line areas of Ukraine, the Federal Council's Ukraine delegate Jacques Gerber announced in Kyiv on Monday 9 November. The money is for evacuations from regions such as Kherson and Donetsk, plus emergency cash, housing, and legal and psychosocial help. It comes out of the CHF 1.5 billion Ukraine programme for 2025–2028.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-11-10-news-swiss-fund-unhcr-evacuations-in-ukraine", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-10", "event_date": "2026-11-09", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Switzerland", "UNHCR", "Ukraine", "Jacques Gerber"]}
{"id": "2026-11-10-news-foreign-banks-rate-switzerland-more-attractive", "date": "2026-11-10", "stream": "news", "headline": "Foreign banks rate Switzerland more attractive", "summary": "More than half of the foreign banks in Switzerland rate it more attractive than three years ago, according to a survey of its 90 members by the Association of Foreign Banks in Switzerland released on Tuesday 10 November.", "url": "https://www.letemps.ch/economie/finance/plus-de-la-moitie-des-banques-etrangeres-jugent-la-suisse-plus-attrayante-qu-il-y-a-trois-ans", "source_domain": "letemps.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["single-source"], "topics": ["switzerland", "economy"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "More than half of the foreign banks in Switzerland rate it more attractive than three years ago, according to a survey of its 90 members by the Association of Foreign Banks in Switzerland released on Tuesday 10 November. They name stability and staff quality as strengths. The weaknesses they cite are no access to the EU market, a technology lag, and rules stricter than international standards (the \"Swiss finish\"). Foreign-owned groups held 83 of the 225 banks in Switzerland at the end of 2025. Some have moved into corporate lending left open by the fall of Credit Suisse.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-11-10-news-foreign-banks-rate-switzerland-more-attractive", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-10", "event_date": "2026-11-10", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Association of Foreign Banks in Switzerland", "Credit Suisse"]}
